Title: Scale Up (add 1 server, LB cluster, split tiers)

ASCII diagram:
[DNS (health-checked)] -> [HAProxy #1]---[HAProxy #2]
           \-> [Web tier] -> [App tier] -> [DB Primary] & [DB Replicas]
Web -> [CDN for static]; App -> [Redis/Memcached cache]

Added & why:
- +1 server and LB cluster (active-active): remove LB SPOF; DNS/VIP failover
- Split components to dedicated servers (Web, App, DB): independent scaling/tuning
- Cache (Redis/Memcached) & CDN: offload DB/app; lower latency, better throughput

Notes:
- Scale up vs Scale out: bigger machine vs more machines (prefer scale out)
- DB: writes to Primary; reads from Replicas; promote Replica on failure
- Keep Web/App stateless (sessions in Redis/JWT) for autoscaling
